},[14,1039,1041],{"id":1040},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[19,1043,1044,1050],{},[23,1045,910,1046,1049],{},[65,1047,1048],{},"luacheck"," for linting",": Catches typos (undeclared globals), unused variables, and unreachable code. Saves hours of debugging.",[55,1052,1053],{"language":57},[59,1054,1056],{"className":61,"code":1055,"language":57,"meta":63,"style":63},"luacheck script.lua\n",[65,1057,1058],{"__ignoreMap":63},[68,1059,1060,1062],{"class":70,"line":71},[68,1061,1048],{"class":81},[68,1063,1064],{"class":85}," script.lua\n",[19,1066,1067,1070,1071,1074],{},[23,1068,1069],{},"Local functions are faster",": ",[65,1072,1073],{},"local function f() end"," is faster and cleaner than assigning to a global.",[19,1076,1077,1080,1081,1084,1085,1088],{},[23,1078,1079],{},"Use descriptive names despite Lua's simplicity",": Lua doesn't have built-in namespacing. Write functions like ",[65,1082,1083],{},"player_update()",", not ",[65,1086,1087],{},"update()",", to avoid collisions.",[19,1090,1091,1094],{},[23,1092,1093],{},"Tables are your data structure",": Every complex data structure (stack, queue, class, closure) uses tables. Learn to manipulate them well.",[14,1096,1098],{"id":1097},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[19,1100,1101,1104,1105,1108,1109,1112,1113,1115],{},[23,1102,1103],{},"Globals leak by default",": Every assignment without ",[65,1106,1107],{},"local"," pollutes the global namespace. Use ",[65,1110,1111],{},"strict.lua"," or a linter to enforce ",[65,1114,1107],{},".",[55,1117,1118],{"language":148},[59,1119,1121],{"className":164,"code":1120,"language":148,"meta":63,"style":63},"x = 5              -- GLOBAL (oops, typo from 'local x = 5')\nlocal y = 10       -- local (safe)\n",[65,1122,1123,1128],{"__ignoreMap":63},[68,1124,1125],{"class":70,"line":71},[68,1126,1127],{},"x = 5              -- GLOBAL (oops, typo from 'local x = 5')\n",[68,1129,1130],{"class":70,"line":78},[68,1131,1132],{},"local y = 10       -- local (safe)\n",[1